# Feature Completion Checklist

A change is **not complete** when only the backend exists. It is complete
when the user-visible path the user actually relies on reaches the new
code, end to end, with tests at the outermost surface and a written trace
in the final response.

This rule generalises `.cursor/rules/connector-checklist.mdc` to all
features: scoring, sensitivity, GUI, reports, exports, pipeline, and
similar. Read `experts/quality/auditor.md` (§S) for the full audit form;
use `audit/templates/feature_completion_matrix.md` as the working artifact.

## When this rule applies

- Any feature that touches more than one module.
- Any change the user described with a literal noun for a surface they
  expect to see (e.g. "Scoring Engine page", "Results tab", "country
  profile", "CLI flag", "report section", "export bundle").
- Any plan submitted via `CreatePlan` for non-trivial implementation work.

## Mandatory steps

1. **Open a Feature Completion Matrix** at
   `audit/feature_completion_matrices/<YYYY-MM-DD>_<slug>.md` from the
   template **before** writing implementation code. Fill the Literal
   Request Check and the End-to-End User Path Diagram first.
2. **Trace the user-visible path** `entry point -> runner -> engine ->
   persistence -> reader/report -> acceptance` and list the concrete file
   for every hop. If any hop is empty, do not start implementation.
3. **Implement every surface** the literal request implies. Anything you
   intend to skip must be marked `Deferred` with explicit user approval
   recorded in the matrix.
4. **Add an outermost-surface test** (GUI / CLI / runner smoke test) that
   would fail if the feature were only implemented in the backend. Pure
   unit tests are not enough.
5. **Add a subtle-consumption check**: every new DB table or CSV must be
   read by an existing or new consumer (Results page, report renderer,
   export). Name the consumer in the matrix.
6. **Cite the trace in the final response.** Paste the one-line path from
   `§8 Final Trace` of the matrix into the response so the user can
   verify the wiring without opening any file.

## Pre-merge self-audit (Definition of Done)

Before claiming completion, run the audit checklist from
`experts/quality/auditor.md` §S in addition to §F. A change does not pass
unless:

- Every row in the Surface Matrix is `Implemented` or `Not applicable`
  (with justification) or `Deferred` (with user approval evidence).
- At least one negative acceptance test exists per user-visible surface.
- The Final Trace covers every hop with a real file path.
- The audit trail and man-hours updates required by
  `.cursor/rules/audit-trail.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/man-hours.mdc` are
  present in the same change.

## Anti-patterns this rule blocks

- "Backend complete, GUI follow-up later" without explicit user approval
  to defer the GUI surface.
- New DB table or CSV with no reader.
- "Tests green" when the tests only exercise pure functions and skip the
  CLI / GUI dispatcher that the user actually invokes.
- Final response that does not include the end-to-end trace.

## Example trace (good)

```
GUI: src/atoms_vs_ashes/gui/screen_pages/04_run_dashboard.py
  -> src/atoms_vs_ashes/gui/_runner.py (start_sensitivity_run --include national)
  -> src/atoms_vs_ashes/scoring/_national_sensitivity.py
  -> national_rank_sensitivity (DB) + audit/.../national_rank_sensitivity.csv
  -> Results page src/atoms_vs_ashes/gui/_results_render_sens.py (national tab)
  -> Country reports report/output/sensitivity/<stamp>/national/<CC>.md
Tests: tests/gui/test_run_dashboard_national.py, tests/scripts/test_phase_1_6_national_sensitivity.py
```
